00:16:16,050 --> 00:16:18,930
...if I can actually do my own laundry...

264
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,020
...there isn't anything I can't do.

265
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,350
That does not sound stupid to me.

266
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:28,650
No, it's like... The first time I had to make dinner for myself after Carol left me...

267
00:16:30,070 --> 00:16:32,940
I'm sorry, that's all the time we have. Next on Ross...

268
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:35,530
Okay.

269
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:36,950
- Uh-oh.     - What, "uh-oh"?

270
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,320
Uh-oh...

271
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:41,450
Uh-oh, the laundry's done.

272
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,620
It's a song.

273
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,710
The laundry song that we sing.

274
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:51,090
Uh-oh, the laundry's done

275
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:52,960
What's the matter?

276
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,300
Nothing. Nothing.

277
00:16:54,550 --> 00:16:55,880
The laundry's done

278
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,220
Come on, show me.

279
00:16:57,470 --> 00:17:01,560
It's just that you left a red sock in with your whites, and now...

280
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:07,400
- ...everything's kind of pink.     - Oh.

281
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:09,310
Everything's pink?

282
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:12,320
Except for the red sock, which is still red.

283
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:15,280
Don't be upset. It can happen to anyone.

284
00:17:15,530 --> 00:17:17,410
But it didn't. It happened to me.

285
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:21,240
God, I'm gonna look like a big Marshmallow Peep!

286
00:17:21,450 --> 00:17:23,290
What am I doing? What am I doing?

287
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:26,710
My father's right! I can't live on my own.

288
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:29,420
I can't even do laundry!

289
00:17:40,930 --> 00:17:42,810
Something went wrong with Underdog...

290
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,270
...and they couldn't get his head to inflate.

291
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,190
So anyway...

292
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:52,230
...his head is, like, flopping down Broadway. Right?

293
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,440
And I'm thinking...

294
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:58,400
...how inappropriate this is.

295
00:17:58,780 --> 00:18:02,780
I've got something's in my eye. Joey, could we check it in the light, please?

296
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,540
- Oh, my God!     - What?

297
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:10,500
Hello! Were we at the same table? It's like...

298
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:13,000
...cocktails in Appalachia.

299
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:21,680
- Come on, they're close.     - Close? She's got her tongue in his ear.

300
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:26,470
Like you've never got a little rambunctious with Ross.

301
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:31,400
Joey, this is sick. It's disgusting. It's...

302
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:33,900
...not really true, is it?

303
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,820
Who's to say what's true?

304
00:18:36,070 --> 00:18:37,150
What were you thinking?

305
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,950
Look, I'm not proud of this, okay?

306
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,610
Well, maybe I am a little.

307
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,490
- Oh.     - Ow!

308
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,580
- I'm out of here!     - Wait! Come on!

309
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,660
You like him. I want her.

310
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:49,330
He likes you.

311
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:52,000
- Really?     - Yeah.

312
00:18:52,250 --> 00:18:55,960
I'm thinking, if we put our heads together, between the two of us...

313
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:58,260
...we can break them up.

314
00:19:01,090 --> 00:19:03,510
I'm so sorry. I can't believe I did this.

315
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:07,220
I just couldn't stop laughing at your Norman Mailer story.

316
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:16,820
Waiter? One more plate of chicken wings over here.

317
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:25,490
Here's the thing. It's like we're different.

318
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:27,700
I'm the bing, you're the boom...

319
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:29,000
- Ow!     - Oh!

320
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,540
- Oh, my God!     - Ow!

321
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:31,790
- I'm so sorry!     - Ow!

322
00:19:32,250 --> 00:19:33,620
- Are you okay?     - Ow!

323
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,880
It's just my lens. It's my lens.

324
00:19:37,670 --> 00:19:39,130
I'll be right back.

325
00:19:41,510 --> 00:19:43,840
I hit her in the eye! I hit her in the eye!

326
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:47,600
This is the worst breakup in the history of the world!

327
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,600
Oh, my God.

328
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:53,190
How many of those have you had?

329
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,610
I don't know. A million!

330
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:59,730
Chandler, shh, shh. Easy, easy. Go to your happy place.

331
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:05,660
- I'm fine, I'm fine.     - All right.

332
00:20:05,870 --> 00:20:07,700
I'm not fine. Here she comes.

333
00:20:07,910 --> 00:20:09,740
Wait here, okay? Breathe.

334
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,060
How do you do that?

335
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:32,350
It's like a gift.

336
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:37,360
We should always, always break up together.

337
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:38,730
I'd like that.

338
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:43,990
You got the clothes clean. That's the important part.

339
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:47,570
I guess. Except everything looks like jammies now.

340
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:54,660
Whoa, I'm sorry.

341
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,420
Excuse me. We had this cart.

342
00:20:58,130 --> 00:21:00,840
I had a 24-inch waist. You lose things.

343
00:21:01,050 --> 00:21:03,340
Now, come on. Get out of my way.

344
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:07,220
I'm sorry. Maybe I wasn't being clear. This was our cart.

345
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:09,470
Hey, hey, hey. There aren't any clothes in it!

346
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,310
Hey, hey, hey! Quit making up rules!

347
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:15,940
Let go! Come on, this is my cart. You know I saw it first.

348
00:21:16,190 --> 00:21:18,400
Listen, Mitzi, if you want this cart...

349
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,150
...you're gonna have to take me with it!

350
00:21:28,450 --> 00:21:30,320
Yes! Did you see that?

351
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,780
You were incredible.

352
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:34,500
A brand-new woman, ladies and gentlemen.

353
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:37,080
I could not have done this without you.

354
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,670
Okay, um...

355
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:47,800
Uh... More clothes in the dryer?

356
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:52,180
- I'm fine. I'm fine.     - Are you sure?

357
00:21:55,890 --> 00:21:58,190
- Are you sure you're okay?     - Yeah.

358
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:00,480
- Does it still hurt?     - Yeah.

359
00:22:03,110 --> 00:22:06,940
What a neat idea. All your clothes match. I'm gonna do this.

360
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:09,740
Hi!

361
00:22:09,950 --> 00:22:10,990
How'd it go?

362
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,240
Excellent!

363
00:22:12,490 --> 00:22:16,750
We ripped that couple apart and kept the pieces for ourselves.

364
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,330
What a beautiful story.

365
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,090
I'm fine, by the way.

366
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:24,670
I'm sorry.

367
00:22:25,170 --> 00:22:28,090
- Where's Chandler?     - He needed some time to grieve.

368
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:30,590
I'm free! I'm free!

369
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,260
That ought to do it.

